
  ┌─ Autoflash emulator, for Windows ───────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ Windows is the computer on the simulated home Wi-Fi PICSimLabWifi (its  │
  │ "Autoflash emulator" adapter is 192.168.60.10). The plug is the         │
  │ emulated stock Sonoff 1.2.0, already paired with your account, at       │
  │ 192.168.60.50.                                                          │
  │                                                                         │
  │ Run the conversion on Windows, exactly as on a real plug:               │
  │     python tools\autoflash.cli.py run                                   │
  │                                                                         │
  │ When it asks you to do something to the plug, do it here:               │
  │     plug restart | plug off | plug on | plug cycle 7    (power)         │
  │ If it asks for your home Wi-Fi: PICSimLabWifi, empty password.          │
  │ Joining the plug's own Wi-Fi from Windows is not emulated.              │
  │                                                                         │
  │ Plug serial log: window "plug" (Ctrl-b n / Ctrl-b p to switch windows). │
  │ Plug web page: http://192.168.60.50 (or http://localhost:8080)          │
  │ Leave: exit every window, or Ctrl-b d. The plug's flash is kept.        │
  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
